+# Worker lifecycle contracts
+
+`worker_lifecycle` defaults to `native_close`. Set `terminal_observation` only
+when the executor has `collaboration.spawn_agent` and `collaboration.list_agents`
+but no close operation. The helper freezes the mode on each reservation; older
+reservations remain native. A configuration edit does not change their evidence.
+
+## Native mode
+
+Use the actual live native spawn schema, await the result, call its real close
+operation, then record `harness spawn-finish <agent> completed|failed --closed`.
+A finished result alone is not closure. Archival and interruption are not closure.
+Do not assert `--closed` if the operation is missing or was not observed.
+
+## Terminal observation mode
+
+After reserve and brief, inspect the returned `worker_task_name`. Launch exactly
+that unique name using the live collaboration schema:
+
+```text
+collaboration.spawn_agent({
+  task_name: <reserved worker_task_name>,
+  model: <reserved model>, reasoning_effort: <reserved effort>,
+  fork_turns: "none",
+  message: "Read and follow your brief: <absolute brief path>"
+})
+```
+
+The brief embeds the role instructions; this API does not automatically load
+named role TOMLs. Pass only fields supported by the actual tool. Confirm the
+real canonical returned name; the helper checks its exact reserved suffix and
+forbids reuse. Wait for completion, then collect a fresh `collaboration.list_agents`
+result. Preserve that real snapshot in the envelope below and record:
+
+```text
+harness spawn-finish <canonical agent name> completed --observation-file <file>
+```
+
+Use outcome `failed` if the completed worker reported a failed task. That releases
+its execution slot but cannot provide successful-role evidence. The supported
+raw terminal status is an object with a nonempty `completed` string. Running,
+unknown, absent, duplicated, or malformed status cannot release the reservation;
+report a blocker if the executor returns another status shape.
+
+```json
+{
+  "source": "collaboration.list_agents",
+  "observed_at": "<actual observation timestamp in ISO 8601 with seconds>",
+  "reservation_id": "<reservation.id>",
+  "goal_key": "<reservation.goal_key>",
+  "run_id": null,
+  "group_id": null,
+  "task_id": null,
+  "rework_cycle": 0,
+  "sha": null,
+  "agent_name": "<actual canonical returned name>",
+  "snapshot": {"agents": [
+    {"agent_name": "<same canonical name>", "agent_status": {"completed": "<real tool result>"}}
+  ]}
+}
+```
+
+The sample nulls are illustrative. Use exact values from the frozen reservation,
+including empty strings or explicit nulls; do not normalize one into the other. Copy the
+actual raw snapshot, not the template or a prior worker's output. MAIN records
+the observation after the tool returns; do not manufacture tool evidence. The
+helper validates matching identities and timestamp bounds atomically, retains
+it in state, and keeps `closed:false`. Repeated identical completion is idempotent;
+changing recorded observation or outcome is rejected. `spawn-finish` atomically
+updates the associated RUNNING task to DONE or FAILED; MAIN records the returned
+handoff and does not need to invent another task-result command.
+
+Once terminally recorded, never steer, resume, or reuse that worker. Every new
+attempt needs a new reservation and unique task name. Its execution slot is
+released, not its addressable conversation thread.
+
+## Recovery
+
+A definitive no-launch `spawn-fail` releases an observer reservation without
+claiming closure. An uncertain launch stays held until confirmed or conclusively
+shown not to have launched. Age, absence, and an aborted call are not proof.
+`reap` refuses active observer reservations. `task retry|cancel` likewise refuses
+an unreleased observer worker; after recording an observed failed outcome, retry
+may create a new reservation. Save a blocker if real terminal evidence is missing.
+
+Successful role/task evidence still requires the current goal/run/group/rework
+identity and, for review/visual gates, the exact implementation commit. Semantic
+failure, an old snapshot, or a configuration change cannot pass those gates.
